---
description: Prevent unnecessary Thinkigen database changes
globs: ["database/**/*"]
alwaysApply: true
---

# MINIMAL CHANGE RULE

The safest database change is the smallest change that fully satisfies the approved requirement.

Do not:
- refactor unrelated code;
- rename for style;
- normalize/denormalize without requirement;
- add indexes just because they might help;
- add audit fields everywhere;
- add status columns when the business rule does not require them;
- add capacity columns;
- add generic tenant IDs;
- add duplicate master data;
- change a datatype without evidence;
- add "future-proof" tables;
- add speculative triggers.

If an optional improvement is valuable, report it as a recommendation instead of implementing it.
